Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250: let expert configurations omit FSL support

Keep the existing defaults while allowing a single-platform ARM firmware
to disable the Freescale-specific driver explicitly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [firmware configuration policy]

--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/Kconfig
@@ -362,7 +362,7 @@
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
 config SERIAL_8250_FSL
-	tristate "Freescale 16550 UART support" if COMPILE_TEST && !(PPC || ARM || ARM64)
+	tristate "Freescale 16550 UART support" if EXPERT || (COMPILE_TEST && !(PPC || ARM || ARM64))
 	depends on SERIAL_8250
 	default SERIAL_8250 if PPC || ARM || ARM64
 	help
